 "genre_note": "132 notes / 18 sub-plans over 20 documents; verified with scripts/verify_cluster_plan.py (PASS: no duplicate (doc,block), no note over 1,800 words, all sub-plans 4-15, coverage 82.7%-97.1%).\n\nBUILDING-BLOCK DISTRIBUTION. As expected for news, the corpus is dominated by empirical_observation (dated events, testimony, quoted statements) and concept (films, products, people, platforms, programmes). argument appears wherever a critic or an expert states a claim with grounds (Polygon's \"Hollywood is in a comedic rut\" framing, the Mario Wonder review's design theses, the DST abolition case, relationship-expert advice). counter_argument is genuinely present and not manufactured: Jacob Lucas rebutting Susan Winter on separations, the NFL rebutting the \"overdoing it\" criticism, Roblox rebutting Gellar, the Cherokee Nation's inaccuracy complaints against Mattel, Sleep School dissenting on clock-change effects, the cardiology finding cited against DST abolition, and the Smiths' repeated denials of open-marriage/divorce/infidelity rumours. model occurs exactly ONCE (doc_0310 [8], the trigger-then-self-perpetuating-worry mechanism of insomnia) \u2014 news almost never states a causal mechanism as such. hypothesis occurs ZERO times: nothing in these 20 documents is framed as a testable prediction, so none was invented. navigation was not produced, per instruction.\n\nTOPICAL-COHERENCE DECISIONS WORTH FLAGGING.\n1. doc_0597 (Polygon, 5,430 words) is a roundup of 26 unrelated films. It became 26 concept notes plus one argument note for the editorial framing. Merging it would have produced a note retrieved for everything and answering nothing. Its three sub-plans are grouped by era/register (classic-Hollywood, action/international, contemporary-indie), which is affinity, not size.\n2. doc_0019 (Fox News) and doc_0068 (White Company advertorial) are the same shape \u2014 8 couples and 6 product sections respectively \u2014 and were split per item for the same reason.\n3. Conversely, doc_0193's twelve slang terms were NOT split: the whole quiz is one subject (~615 words), and splitting it would fragment \"what did Scorsese say X means?\" across notes. Size did not drive that decision either way.\n4. Shared-entity notes carry blocks from several documents where the same subject recurs: the Smiths' 2023 separation disclosure draws on all four Independent Smith articles; Swift/Kelce origin, Swift's Chiefs attendance, and Swift's attitude to scrutiny each draw on both doc_0046 and doc_0295; the Federline marriage, child-support disputes and the Asghari marriage each draw on both doc_0051 and doc_0358.\n\nBLOCKS I ALMOST DROPPED AND DID NOT. doc_0310 [19] (Dr Browning saying there is \"no harm in trying the occasional Reddit recommendation \u2014 if it's free\") reads like a throwaway sign-off but is a scope condition that partly reverses the article's own attack on sleep hacks; it is assigned to the \"why quick fixes fail\" note rather than dropped. doc_0339 [31] (Sleep School declaring itself \"impartial\" on whether clock changes affect sleep) contradicts the section it sits inside and is kept as its own counter_argument note. doc_0339 [42] (a YouGov poll showing Britons marginally FAVOUR keeping DST) undercuts the article's abolition framing and is kept inside the abolition-campaign note. doc_0036 [5] leads with the children but carries Jada's claim that the marriage was \"never an open one\"; it is assigned by its dominant subject rather than discarded.\n\nCOVERAGE HONESTY. Two documents land in the 82-86% band for structural, not editorial, reasons. doc_0018 (82.7%) is a year-by-year timeline whose eleven one-line date headers plus two photo captions are pure section chrome. doc_0339 (85.1%) and doc_0019 (86.1%) are similarly header-heavy \u2014 doc_0019 additionally carries 10 all-caps \"read more\" cross-promo headlines, WATCH links, \"APP USERS CLICK HERE\" and a newsletter sign-up line. doc_0068 is a sponsored advertorial for The White Company; its notes are honest product-catalogue descriptions rather than reporting, and the sub-plan title says so. Everything else clears 87%, and the two Polygon documents clear 94%."
}